The '''Great Schism of 1615''', also known as the '''Great Schism''', the '''Caphiric Schism''', and the '''Great Occidental Schism''', was a split within the [[Catholic Church]] lasting from 1615 to 2017 in which the [[Caphiric Church|Caphiric Catholic Church]] broke away from the authority of the [[Pope]] and the [[Catholic Church]]. The schism was the culmination of theological and political differences developed during the preceding centuries between the wider Catholic community and Caphiria and the Imperators

