The '''Judiciary of Cartadania''' is the judicial branch of the [[federal government of Cartadania]], encompassing all courts operating under federal jurisdiction and distinct from the state and territorial judicial systems. Its structure is established under Article 3 of the [[Constitution of Cartadania]], which provides the framework for the judiciary’s role, authority, and independence. Federal courts operate within a [[Law of Cartadania|common law system]], where judicial decisions establish binding precedents that shape the interpretation and application of laws. The judiciary is further governed by the [[Law of Cartadania|Code of Cartadania]], which outlines procedural and substantive legal principles.

