'''Auraicum''' was a province of [[Great Levantia]] situated along the upper [[Auara River]] basin, with its northern borders based on the [[Calidus River|Calidus]] and [[Maruva River]]s while its southern perimeter sat along the [[Chrisos River]] and the highland elevation of central Dericania. It roughly corresponds to the eastern half of [[Rhotia]] though it crossed into northeastern [[Lapody]] as well. The province was established in the wake of the campaigns of [[Gaius Stephanus Pictor]], who established [[Colpira|Colonia Pictoria]] as a preliminary staging area for Levantine conquests during the [[Caballian Wars]]. Colonia Pictoria was the seat of the provincial administration, though for a time [[Pusego]] overshadowed it in terms of economic relevance. Auraicum was primarily connected to the rest of Great Levantia by the ''[[Via Nauria]]'', which crossed the central Dericanian steppe and connected the [[Norteven River]] to the Auara's tributary of the [[Nauros River]]. The [[Allarii]] were the major [[foederati]] group in the province, residing close to the western border.

