'''Boregonia''' was a province of [[Great Levantia]] encompassing the [[Ile Burgundie]] in modern [[Burgundie]]. It was conquered from [[Albagubria]] [[Campaigns_of_Gnaeus_I#Conquest_of_Albagubria|during the early second century]]. Two of its major cities - [[Vilauristre|Parapeion]] and [[Port Diteaux|Nordarmus]] - were a part of the [[Decapolis]]. A third, [[Colonia Bruganicum]], was established by the general Julian Marcilius Corvus when he subdued the island in the first decade of the second century. Boregonia was gradually integrated into the broader cultural Levantine culture, a culture which developed the [[Littoric language]], Vulgar Latin influenced by [[Galatids|Galatid]] and [[Ancient Istroyan civilization|ancient Istroyan]] vocabulary. Due to its relatively small confines, the province had no [[foederati]] and was heavily populated by both Latins and Istroyans.

