The '''Decapolis''' was a group of ten major [[Ancient Istroyan civilization|ancient Istroyan]] city-states on the southeastern coast of [[Levantia]] and generally describes ancient Istroya's Levantine component. Despite its name, it also included a number of minor cities and trade outposts and extended from roughly [[Telpól]] in the southwest to most of [[Burgundie]] in the northeast. These cities specialized in trade, specifically facilitating {{Wp|transshipment}} of some goods between [[Sarpedon]] and [[Audonia]]. In addition to transshipment, trade with the indigenous [[Galatids|Galatid]] peoples became an increasingly large part of the Decapolis's economic activity, including buying raw materials from the Galatids as well as slaves for export to Audonia. The cities were loosely allied together for common defense starting in about the year 600 BC, though traders and groups within the cities frequently engaged in rivalry and conflict over trade rights within the Levantine interior. In addition to the cities themselves, the Decapolis included a larger network of Celtic tribes who served alternatively

